I saw mention of a hack (no pun intended) on the newsgroup to make your
prayer timeout appear on the bottom line, along with the rest of your stats.
After a careful 5 minute inspection of the code, I made the correction
necessary, and now I know what my god thinks of me! If you:

- care
- feel like messing with it
- can recompile the source
- don't feel like this is cheating

you can grab the included patchfile and use patch<patchfile in your nethack
source directory (.../nethack_top/src) to make this small change to botl.c.

I guess someone might accuse this file of being a spoiler, so here goes the
obligatory ^L...


path for botl.c (botl.c.patch)
This patch causes the prayer timeout to be displayed at the lower right hand
side of the lower status line, right after "Exp:" or "T:", depending on your
options. When prayer timeout reaches zero, it's okay to pray again. Apply
patch by doing the following:

Save this message to a file.
Strip out everything above and below (and including) the "snip" lines.
name the file botl.c.patch.
move this file to your nethack source directory.
cd to the nethack source directory.
Type the following command: patch < botl.c.patch
remake nethack (You should be able to just type "make" in the src directory)

Enjoy.

------------------8<-----snip--------8<-----------------
*** botl.c.orig	Thu May 26 13:49:41 1994
--- botl.c	Thu May 26 13:20:56 1994
***************
*** 407,412 ****
--- 407,414 ----
  	Sprintf(nb = eos(nb), " Exp:%u", u.ulevel);
  	if(flags.time)
  	    Sprintf(nb = eos(nb), " T:%ld", moves);
+ /* This prints the prayer timeout on the status line. JSH 05/26/94 */
+     Sprintf(nb = eos(nb), " Pray:%u", u.ublesscnt);
  	if(strcmp(hu_stat[u.uhs], "        ")) {
  		Sprintf(nb = eos(nb), " ");
  		Strcat(newbot2, hu_stat[u.uhs]);
